      long_en: "A high tower is a tall structure, sometimes the height of a multi-storey building, that sends targets far above the shooter. Very high targets are slower to read and need confident gun movement, so they separate top shooters from the rest. Because of the height, the shot fall area is large, which matters for safety and for where spectators can stand. Some grounds use a hill top instead of a tower to get the same effect.",
