      long_en: "A clay target is made of a mixture of pitch or resin and chalk (or of biodegradable material) and breaks when hit by shot. Despite the name, it contains no clay. Sporting uses several shapes and sizes — standard, midi, mini, battue, rabbit — and different colours. Shooters and referees often simply say «bird», because the targets imitate game.",
